    "evidence": "Comprehensive evidence with specific citations, effect sizes, and implementation science research: Transitional care interventions (TCIs) significantly reduce all-cause readmissions (RR: 0.78; 95% CI: 0.70\u20130.86) and HF-specific readmissions (RR: 0.73; 95% CI: 0.64\u20130.83) [1, 3]. Telephone support, multidisciplinary teams, and home visits are effective TCI components [1, 3, 4]. The Consolidated Framework for Implementation Research (CFIR) provides a structure for implementing TCIs effectively [6]. Implementation science research highlights the importance of health equity integration and tailored strategies for successful implementation [7, 8, 9].",
    "health_equity": "Dedicated section addressing health disparities, cultural adaptation, and equity considerations for this protocol: This protocol explicitly integrates health equity principles by promoting culturally adapted communication, mandatory provider training on cultural humility and bias, engagement of community health workers, systematic screening for and addressing of social determinants of health (SDOH), and disparity-focused quality improvement through data stratification and equity-focused metrics. Clinical pharmacists play a key role in addressing medication access barriers and providing culturally sensitive medication adherence support.",
