      "considerations": [
        "**Population-Specific Validation:** The psychometric properties of screening tools can vary significantly across different populations (e.g., age, gender, ethnicity, clinical setting). It is crucial to use tools validated for the specific adolescent population being screened.",
        "**Cut-off Scores:** Optimal cut-off scores for screening tools may differ based on the desired balance between sensitivity and specificity, and the prevalence of depression in the population. Local validation and clinical judgment are important.",
        "**Brief vs. Comprehensive Tools:** While brief tools are suitable for initial screening, more comprehensive diagnostic interviews are necessary for confirming a diagnosis of depression.",
        "**Integration into Workflow:** Screening tools should be easily integrated into existing primary care workflows to minimize burden on clinicians and maximize uptake.",
        "**Training:** Healthcare providers require adequate training on the administration, scoring, and interpretation of screening tools, as well as on appropriate follow-up actions."
      ],
