    "protocol_title": "Community Health - Health Promotion Campaign Development Protocol",
    "introduction": "This protocol outlines a comprehensive, evidence-based approach to developing health promotion campaigns specifically targeting Medicaid populations. The purpose is to guide the creation of effective, equitable, and culturally adapted campaigns that address health disparities and improve health outcomes within this vulnerable demographic. The protocol integrates insights from implementation science, health equity frameworks, and established evaluation methodologies.",
